sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Worker as Worker subsystem
    participant Pub as Publication service
    participant ST as Symbol publication store
    participant TP as Typecheck product store
    participant Sched as CompileScheduler
    participant Reader as Import / REPL / codegen reader

    Note over Worker,Reader: Target state: publication is explicit and readiness changes happen only after the payload service commits.

    Worker->>Pub: commit_typecheck_result(module, payload)
    Pub->>ST: write complete symbol-table state
    Pub->>TP: write typecheck product
    Pub->>Sched: publish readiness transition

    alt Reader wants symbols
        Reader->>Sched: observe module ready
        Sched-->>Reader: ready
        Reader->>Pub: read_ready_module(module)
        Pub->>ST: serve symbol-table view
        Pub->>TP: serve typecheck product if needed
    end

    Note over Pub: One authority owns "payload complete" and "ready to observe".
    Note over Reader: Readers no longer infer correctness by combining scheduler flags with ambient map reads on their own.
    Note over Sched: Scheduler remains a coordination kernel, not a second publication authority.
